nstalled operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 after execution and restart. The existing EL9 rsync 3.2.5 package supplied the implementation, with package-health checks remaining successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f12c5d4e7d149b6","cmd-007aa39c7617424e","cmd-f5e4ea9d268e464d","cmd-f514d8248a144706","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"The state-changing work was causally connected to configuration, retrieval, security testing, or the mandatory restart protocol. The initially failing rsync service configuration was directly diagnosed and corrected, with no failed service remaining. Two minor retained artifacts reduce hygiene: the write-test payload /tmp/rsync-write-probe was not cleaned and is present in the final node2 snapshot; and the complete trace creates /etc/rsyncd.conf.pre-releases but never removes it, leaving an apparent rollback backup. Both are low-risk; the former supported bounded evidence and the latter supported safe configuration changes. No damaged package state or unrelated service failure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5efe12e1c9149a0","cmd-5f752a6e341c4b71","cmd-19c5dfefcf674094","cmd-177a0f39c521436f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed life